# Laravel conventions

## Structure

- Controllers: route handling only — delegate to Actions or Services.
- Form Requests for validation; Policies for authorization.
- Eloquent models in `app/Models/`; avoid fat models — extract complex logic.

## Patterns

```php
// ❌ BAD — validation and logic in controller
public function store(Request $request) {
    $request->validate(['email' => 'required|email']);
    User::create($request->only('email'));
}

// ✅ GOOD — Form Request + Action
public function store(StoreUserRequest $request, CreateUserAction $action) {
    return UserResource::make($action->execute($request->validated()));
}
```

## Database

- Eager-load relationships to prevent N+1 (`User::with('posts')->get()`).
- Migrations must be reversible when feasible.
- Use factories in tests; never seed production data from tests.

## Do not

- Call `env()` outside `config/` files.
- Put business logic in Blade views (API-only projects: no Blade business logic).
- Use raw SQL when Eloquent covers the case.
